      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "EXAMPLE · KLING IMAGE 4.0 LONG IMAGE → 6 SECTIONS\n\n1. Open \"Kling 3.0 Full · API Key\": enter your own Kling API key OR leave blank if KLING_API_KEY is configured on the server. Never share a workflow with a real key embedded.\n2. Select a PRODUCT PHOTO in the Load Image node. Ecommerce mode requires at least one reference_1 image (prefer a clear 300px+ studio product image).\n3. In Long Image, leave skill=ecommerce; choose length=medium and resolution=2k. Set the preview dropdown to ALLOW only when you are ready for a possibly billable API request.\n4. Press Queue. The image output is the FULL LONG PAGE. The sections output is a batch of 6 equally tall local crops (controlled by section_count).\n5. Each Save Image node writes to a subfolder of ComfyUI/output. Six section files are saved automatically; no six separate Kling requests.\n\nNOTE: sections are CROPS of the same page, not independently generated or semantically separated images. Changing section_count via the local Split Long Image utility does not consume Kling credits. Generated copy/claims need human review."
      ],
      "title": "HOW TO USE · Long Image to individual sections"
    }
